  "limits": [
    "Ten managed raw control/release cases and fourteen native-span cases, each through an independent importing process on ZeroMQ or gRPC.",
    "Actual native CPU-L1 gather, per-key admission, host checksums, unaligned positional restore and a second same-position restore from unchanged canonical bytes. Source writes are submitted behind outstanding device work.",
    "Same request-generation retries do not resubmit native work. Foreign clients and altered handles refuse before transfer; corruption and eviction refuse before scatter.",
    "Failed admission and stale publication return no reusable span. A failure after real native enqueue retains physical debt when drain is refused; later server-device drain permits cleanup without re-enqueueing.",
    "Device errors and drain refusals are controlled injections, not recovery from a real device fault. Client-declared artifact identities are not model attestation.",
    "One worker, full BF16 attention and CPU L1 only. Loaded-needs-repair does not authorize computed model tokens. No model outputs, NVMe I/O, GDS, DMA-BUF comparison or performance claim."
